abstract: "Dirichlet Weight Regularization (dreg) — a scale-invariant Riemannian Rayleigh 2D Dirichlet penalty with parameter-weighted layer aggregation that breaks permutation symmetry, compacts >91% of Attention and FFN 2D-DCT spectral energy below rho <= 0.40, and pairs with zero-overhead MSE-clipped / Lloyd-Max Base-3 Trit quantization (.tritq). Multi-seed (N=3) 10k-step experiments on TinyStories-10M achieve 16.87 +/- 1.73 PPL at 1.638 bpp (4.04x lower than standard TritQ, 2.19x lower than Group INT2 g=64 at 27% fewer bits) and 95.60 +/- 28.26 PPL at sub-1-bit 0.914 bpp (11.4x lower). Pre-trained GPT-2 (124M) rayleigh_sg adaptation cuts roughness by 95.6% and lowers compressed perplexity 23x-77x across 1.63-3.77 bpp, backed by a portable C11 direct spectral matvec micro-kernel (13.0 KB SRAM, 650x reduction)."
